      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since perpendicular lines have slopes that are negative reciprocals of each other, the slope of ${l}_{2}$ is the negative reciprocal of the slope of ${l}_{1}.$ Since ${l}_{1}$ has a slope of $-4,$ the line ${l}_{2}$ must have a slope of $\\frac{1}{4}.$\n\nOur perpendicular line must have the slope $m=\\frac{1}{4}$ and a $y$-intercept of $-5.$ Therefore, it can be written in slope-intercept form as\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{4}x-5.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy"
    },
